  "prefLabel": "Nat 103.06 Quorum and Majority for Decision Making",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Nat 103.06 Quorum and Majority for Decision Making.\n\n(a) A total of 3 members of the board shall constitute a quorum, in accordance with RSA 328-E:7, V, to convene a meeting or conduct a hearing.\n\n(b) Any action shall be taken only by the affirmative vote of a majority of those board members present and voting.\n\n(c) Board members shall inform the board administrator at the earliest possible time if they will be unable to attend a meeting so that a new meeting time can be scheduled if there will not be a quorum.\n\nSource. #6379, eff 11-26-96; ss by #8299, eff 3-9-05; ss by #13139, eff 11-26-20; ss by #14392, eff 9-30-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/nat100-700.html"
